cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool, please cite it as below."
title: "orcid-finder"
abstract: >-
  A static, client-side web tool that finds the ORCID accounts declaring an
  institution, searching by ROR, GRID and Ringgold identifiers and by
  organisation name, and narrowing them by keyword, current or past affiliation,
  role title, department, country, start date, and whether the employment was
  asserted by a member organisation rather than self-declared. It reports which
  filter dropped each candidate and exports the result as CSV or JSON together
  with the query that produced it. Multilingual (EN/DE/ES). Runs entirely in the
  browser against the public ORCID and ROR APIs: no account, no API key, no
  backend.
type: software
